    <div class="p4-section-label">Phase 4 Architecture</div>
    <h2 class="p4-section-title">Rail-driven pistons → transmission → wheels</h2>
    <p class="p4-section-lead">
        Phase 4 inverts the piston-rail relationship. A central pressure-driven rail
        reciprocates linearly (forward/backward). Stationary pistons sit along this
        rail's path. As the rail moves, it pushes the pistons into a transmission coupling.
        The transmission converts this linear push into rotational wheel drive. Pistons
        never move—the rail does all the work. Result: open, clean, contamination-free
        power transfer.
    </p>

